{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And Abraham prayed to Elohim.</b> By way of the Kabbalah: 'to Elohim' is the tenth attribute, and therefore it immediately says 'and Elohim healed,' because the attribute of judgment was transformed into the attribute of mercy — for HaShem had restrained him with the attribute of mercy, which was turned back upon him into judgment. And if you will look wisely into the supernal verses, you will see that it first says ״ויבא אלהים אל אבימלך בחלום הלילה״ — 'and Elohim came to Abimelech in a dream of the night' — for the Shekhinah revealed itself to him for Abraham's honor. Therefore he prayed in the name אל\"ף דל\"ת and said ״אדני הגוי גם צדיק תהרוג״ — 'Adonai, will you slay even a righteous nation?' — and he justified himself in the whole matter when the Shekhinah revealed itself to him in the dream; as it says ״ויאמר אליו האלהים בחלום״ — 'and Elohim said to him in the dream' — mentioning it with the definite article, and spoke with him and said to him ״גם אנכי ידעתי כי בתם לבבך״ — 'even I knew that in the integrity of your heart' — that is, you say 'in the integrity of my heart and in the innocence of my hands I did this,' and you who know — even I knew, for I am the Knower and the Witness, and I will restrain you, even I. The verse's explanation of ״ואחשוך גם אנכי אותך״ — 'and I restrained you, even I' — is that even from the supernal cause, which is the One who is hidden, there came to him prevention of sin. And this is why it says ״אנכי״ and not ״אני״, from what you know by way of the Kabbalah, that ״אנכי״ is more inward than ״אני״ because of the added כ\"ף. And perhaps for this reason the אל\"ף was hidden from the word מחטא (from sinning), and the verse explains to you that one who sins against Elohim sins against the One who is hidden, and all who rebel against Him rebel against the Name that is unique within him:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The comment ends with a trailing colon (ואמר / leading shape), here marked by the colon at the end; preserved as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:57.427392755Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}